# Web UX contract

Follow `docs/ux/web-ux-conventions.md` (source of truth). Digest:

- Bottom nav has 5 stable tabs: Home, Transactions, Resources, Customers, More. Do not add/remove tabs without updating that doc.
- Transactions = Orders + cash Loans in the UI only; keep rentals and money_loans engines separate.
- Global actions always include Search, New Order, Return, Add Resource, Scan.
- Thumb-zone primary actions; one dominant choice per step; list/status-first (no chart dashboards in MVP).
- Status colors: Available green, Rented blue, Due Today orange, Overdue red, Archived grey.
- Offline: subtle non-blocking banner only. More-tab offline toggle is demo/simulation, not product positioning.
- Appearance: Dark/Light only; default Dark; More-tab segmented toggle; theme-aware colors via ColorScheme (no light-only hardcodes).
- Forms: items-first New Order (running total; days/amount happy path; Rent/Sell/Job under More options gated by template enabled resource types; do not hide catalog by type), then phone-first customer attach with optional collapsed Advance; skip customer when issuing from a profile; unit identity optional unless catalog requires it.
- Home defaults: search + KPIs + needsAttention (template presets may add recentActivity / pendingJobs; Quick Actions via Customize Home; FAB for New Order / Return).
